{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Stormbringer: Forked Lightning transforms into Thunder Wave (#2802)",
  "contract": "#2802 Thunder Wave 705692 (Spell.dbc, server set /srv/coa/server-data/dbc): PASSIVE, ProcFlags 0, ProcChance 5 (the tooltip's $h), Effect[0] APPLY_AURA with SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL and EffectTriggerSpell 712353. ProcFlags 0 with no spell_proc row makes SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs skip the spell (SpellMgr.cpp:2255-2257), so the aura was never offered a proc; and 712353 'Thunder Wave' is a bare 10 s self SPELL_AURA_DUMMY that no code reads, so even a proc entry would have delivered nothing. The real payload is 707220 'Thunder Wave', the spell the talent's Description embeds as @s:707220:0@: Effect[0] SCHOOL_DAMAGE with EffectBasePoints 405 + EffectDieSides 48 and EffectRealPointsPerLevel 1.65 (the tooltip's 406 at its base level), SchoolMask 72 (Nature|Arcane = Spellstorm), TargetB 16 DEST_AREA_ENEMY with EffectRadiusIndex 29 = 6 yd, and Effect[1] SPELL_EFFECT_ASCENSION_REFRESH_AURA with EffectMiscValue 500928 (Volt) and EffectBasePoints 17999 + EffectDieSides 1 = 18000 ms, which is Volt's own SpellDuration id 85. Damage dealt by Forked Lightning 501438 now rolls the talent's own ProcChance of 5 and casts 707220 at the victim on success, at most once per Forked Lightning cast. The payload leg is deterministic and passes before and after the fix (BASELINE): it casts 707220 by hand on a Volt-affected dummy whose Volt was left to decay, and shows the native refresh put it back to 18000 ms. The proc leg is statistical, as the README requires for a chance below 100%: one dummy takes 120 Forked Lightning casts, so a fix that never fires fails with probability 1 - 0.95^100 > 99.4% even if a tenth of the casts are dropped, while the unfixed server can only ever reach the single hand-cast Thunder Wave.",
